 "web": "These barriers land on the same child at once. One pattern: a mother working hourly loses her child-care subsidy in a county enrollment freeze (Barrier 6); a report is made and the finding is neglect (Barrier 3); the child goes to a grandmother whose support was cut (Barrier 5), who arrives at the school office without the paper that lets her sign for him (Barrier 8) and puts his first bed and winter coat on a credit card (Barrier 9); the child's trauma shows up as behavior his school cannot hold, and the wait for a facility-school seat is months (Barrier 2); a residential bed would help, but the nearest is out of state (Barrier 1); the adults who could help him most leave the field because the pay is low (Barrier 4). No one barrier decided his life. Together they set the price.",
